Q: How to print the data from each row of a query in CodeIgniter A: <pre><code>public function getUserForAdmin() { 
    $arrayUser = $this-&gt;bdd-&gt;getArray('SELECT prenom AS prenomUFA, nom AS nomUFA, email AS emailUFA, cp AS cpUFA FROM user');
    return $arrayUser;
}
</code></pre>

<p>In index.php call it like this  -</p>

<pre><code>$userForAdmin = $user-&gt;getUserForAdmin();
foreach($userForAdmin as $rows)
{  
    echo '&lt;p&gt;'.$rows['prenomUFA'].'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;';
    echo '&lt;p&gt;'.$rows['nomUFA'].'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;';
    echo '&lt;p&gt;'.$rows['emailUFA'].'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;';
    echo '&lt;p&gt;'.$rows['cpUFA'].'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;';
}
</code></pre>

<p>Above code outputs all the values.</p>

